    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO PROVIDE FOR THE REPEAL OF THE DEBITS TAXACT, NO. 16 OF 2002",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      261.55,
      401.69,
      286.89
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      297.55,
      401.65,
      322.89
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Debits Tax (Repeal) Act,No. of 2011.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      333.55,
      401.81,
      358.89
    ],
    "text": "2.(1) The Debits Tax Act, No. 16 of 2002 is herebydeemed to be repealed with effect from March 31, 2011.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      369.55,
      402.05,
      418.89
    ],
    "text": "(2) The provisions of this Act shall, notwithstanding suchrepeal, in respect of the matters set out in subsection (3), be inforce for a period of three years from the date of the cominginto operation of this Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      429.55,
      402.06,
      454.89
    ],
    "text": "(3) Notwithstanding the repeal of the Debits Tax Act, No.16 of 2002 with effect from March 31, 2011:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      177.57,
      465.55,
      402.07,
      598.89
    ],
    "text": "(a)the debits tax imposed under section 2 of therepealed Act, with effect from April 1, 2011, to theday immediately preceding the day on which theoperation of the period of three years specified insubsection (2) expires, be collected by everylicensed commercial bank or specialised bank orevery financial institution in terms of section 5 ofthe repealed Act and all sums so recovered by everysuch bank and financial institution as debits taxshall be remitted to the Commissioner-General interms of section 6 of the repealed Act ; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      177.57,
      609.55,
      401.84,
      670.89
    ],
    "text": "(b)any action, proceeding or matter filed under theprovisions of the Debits Tax Act, No. 16 of 2002prior to its repeal, shall notwithstanding such repeal,with effect from April 1, 2011, be continued untilthey are concluded :",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
